today we're talking about final fantasy  14 hitting the pause button on sales as  well as new world getting a huge update  and more  since the release of the game's end  walker expansion long queues to get into  the game server have been a headache for  both players and devs in response to the  long wait time square enix released  another announcement with what steps  it's taking to address the congestion  unexpectedly square enix will now  temporarily suspend sales of both final  fantasy xiv's base game and the complete  edition free trial registration for new  accounts will also be put on hold as  well as new advertisements it's unknown  how long this policy will last for but  the company will continue to monitor the  situation as they consider the timing  around resuming sales square enix once  again reassured players it's trying to  get more hardware and equipment in order  to expand server capacity due to the  global shortage of the materials needed  adding a new logical data center and  more worlds will not be instantaneous  the company hopes to have a roadmap in  late january for server expansion  and speaking of mmos let's talk about  another game that had a rough launch new  world the winter convergence festival is  now live and is the game's first  seasonal event from december 16th to  january 11th you can earn winter tokens  from repeatable quests across eternum to  earn exclusive new armor weapons and  more as players look to stop the evil  winter warrior from plunging the land  into the dreaded forever winter as  someone that hates winter a forever  winter sounds terrifying but the game's  ice-themed event is just the tip of the  iceberg when it comes to changes in new  world's most recent update nearly every  aspect of new world has been touched in  some way from weapon balancing to  crafting tweaks dramatic changes to end  game content and gearing are perhaps the  most notable the patch introduces the  new expertise system one that requires  max level players to raise their  expertise level on a per gear slot basis  in order to get maximum efficiency out  of equipped items the system was  initially met with widespread criticism  from the new world community but after  some adjustments to make it so craft  gear or items acquired from quest would  not apply to the new expertise rules  players seem to have more readily  accepted the change the game also  introduces a new end-game crafting  component called gypsum this component  is earned from participating in a  variety of in-game activities which  should give players more agency when it  comes to improving their gear and  expertise levels the full list of patch  notes is very long so make sure you head  over to gamespot.com to see all of the  changes  and sticking with multiplayer games call  of duty vanguard is having a free  multiplayer weekend that starts today  december 16th as part of the trial  anyone can get access to vanguard's  multiplayer across all platforms players  will have double xp enabled and they'll  get rewarded with battle pass tier skips  and an xp boost if they upgrade to the  full game playlists included in the free  access are the free kills playlist which  will be a mix of team deathmatch  domination and hardpoint the champions  hill playlist which is vanguard's  gunfight style tournament mode and  following an update later in the day on  december 16th a third playlist will go  live shipments 24 7. this will featured  mixed game modes on the holiday map  reskin of shipment so are you upset  about this final fantasy news let me  know in the comments below i'll see you  tomorrow  [Music]  [Music]
 

